<note version="0.3" xmlns:link="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy/link" xmlns:size="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy/size" xmlns="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy">
  <title>meson build</title>
  
<text xml:space="preserve"><note-content version="0.1"><underline>meson build</underline>
A tip for your future compilations

After building, you can always ask Meson what it's going to install:

meson install -C build --dry-run

or simply inspect:

meson introspect build --installed

It will show every file the project intends to install. It's a great way to learn how a project is structured.



Since you're on Debian Sid...

I think you'd enjoy adopting this workflow:

meson setup build
meson compile -C build
sudo meson install -C build
sudo ldconfig

or, if the project still documents Ninja directly:

meson setup build
ninja -C build
sudo ninja -C build install
sudo ldconfig

It becomes muscle memory, and you avoid exactly the kind of "works in the build directory but not after copying" issues you just ran into.
</note-content></text>
